From 81e10aa37eeee511dd760c4ba08c141791d751f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:12:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/39] videocontrols: surface media errors for audio-only
 content
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

setupStatusFader hid the status overlay for isAudioOnly unconditionally, which also hid
the ERROR state — so an <audio> whose format cannot be decoded (MP3/AAC have no decoder
in this build; err=4 MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED) rendered a live-looking control bar with
no failure shown (the forbidden works-looking-but-silent shape, gre-widgets R1). Keep the
throbber/loading suppression but let a genuine, non-suppressed video.error surface for
audio-only too. Normal decodable audio is untouched. Device-verified: MP3 <audio> now shows
the X + 'format is not supported' overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.xml | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.xml b/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.xml
index 18f82569fd..c118110536 100644
--- a/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.xml
+++ b/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.xml
@@ -337,7 +337,14 @@
 
                     // Explicitly hide the status fader if this
                     // is audio only until bug 619421 is fixed.
-                    if (this.isAudioOnly)
+                    // Jihad: upstream suppressed the overlay for audio-only content (no video box
+                    // to draw a throbber over), but it also hid the ERROR state — so an <audio>
+                    // whose format cannot be decoded (MP3/AAC have no decoder in this build; the
+                    // element ends err=4 MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED) rendered a live-looking
+                    // control bar with no failure shown: the forbidden "works-looking but silent"
+                    // shape (cavekit-gre-widgets.md R1). Keep the throbber/loading suppression, but
+                    // let a real, non-suppressed media error still surface for audio-only too.
+                    if (this.isAudioOnly && !(this.video.error && !this.suppressError))
                         show = false;
 
                     this.log("Status overlay: seeking=" + this.video.seeking +
-- 
